      plan:["Mở bài: paraphrase + nói bài bàn về nguyên nhân và hậu quả","Thân 1: nguyên nhân (công nghệ thay đổi nhanh, gia đình sống tách biệt)","Thân 2: hậu quả (người già cô đơn, mất đi kinh nghiệm/truyền thống)","Kết bài: tóm tắt, gợi ý ngắn"],
      model:"In many modern societies, elderly people do not receive the same respect that they did in previous generations. This essay will explain why this has happened and what effects it has on society.\n\nThere are two main causes. Firstly, technology is changing very quickly. In the past, older people were respected because they had the most knowledge and experience. Today, however, young people can find information on the internet in seconds, so they may feel that they do not need advice from their grandparents. Secondly, family structures have changed. Many young adults move to big cities for work, so they no longer live with their parents and grandparents, and they spend less time with them.\n\nThis situation has several negative effects. The most serious is that many old people feel lonely and unwanted, which can damage their mental and physical health. In addition, society loses valuable knowledge. For example, traditional skills such as cooking, farming or making handicrafts are often passed from one generation to the next, and these skills may disappear if young people are not interested in learning them. Families may also become weaker, because children and grandparents have fewer chances to share their experiences and understand each other.\n\nIn conclusion, the fast pace of technology and changes in family life are the main reasons why older people are less respected today. This can lead to loneliness and the loss of traditions, so schools and families should encourage young people to spend more time with the older generation."
